    karr --version    # "Unknown option: version", exit 2

Every .pm and bin/karr carry `our $VERSION`, `karr skill check` compares versions, bug reports ask for one, and kanban-md's binary answers `--version`. karr has no way to print its own.

## What to build

`karr --version` prints `karr <version>` on stdout and exits 0. The flag only, no `version` subcommand: it is what cobra offers and what people type. Keep the parsing in App::karr next to `--dir`/`--help`, list it under OPTIONS in `karr --help`, and make sure it works through the Docker alias (`docker run ... karr --version`). Changes entry, test.

Pointers: lib/App/karr.pm. option done (around line 185) is the model for a root option, _print_help (around line 255) for the OPTIONS block, and the argv scan near line 328 is what lets a root option precede the command. The number is $App::karr::VERSION. t/131-help-column-alignment.t shows how the root command is driven from a test without a board.

